codex
Both modules are implemented. J8 now retains exact-length J2 alternatives and separate J4 overlap/exact summaries, with input hashes and row-count checks. J10 computes tied-rank agreement and pair-order reversals, calls evaluation_core’s metric guards, and blocks channel nulls when decoy scores are unavailable. I’m checking edge cases and preparing the bounded job scripts.
